pseudo-Boolean proof version 3.0
% Pigeonhole: four variables, three values, all_different.  The whole
% refutation is two cutting-planes additions.  There is no search.
%
% Step 1: each variable takes at least one value.  That is a consequence of the
% direct-atom definitions rather than an axiom of the model, so we derive it.
% Summing the "_dn" rows makes every order atom cancel against its own
% negation, and what survives is exactly the at-least-one row.
@atleast1 pol @x1eq0_dn @x1eq1_dn + @x1eq2_dn + ;
@atleast2 pol @x2eq0_dn @x2eq1_dn + @x2eq2_dn + ;
@atleast3 pol @x3eq0_dn @x3eq1_dn + @x3eq2_dn + ;
@atleast4 pol @x4eq0_dn @x4eq1_dn + @x4eq2_dn + ;
% Step 2: four variables need four values, and only three exist.  Adding the
% three at-most-one rows to the four at-least-one rows cancels every atom and
% leaves 0 >= 1.
pol @amo1_0 @amo1_1 + @amo1_2 + @atleast1 + @atleast2 + @atleast3 + @atleast4 + ;
output NONE;
conclusion UNSAT;
end pseudo-Boolean proof;
